// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the Unreal asset pack text > guide snapshot 1`] = `
"# Test prop — Unreal import guide

#001 This pack is a derived artifact of a mojulo recipe (\`recipe/sk_test-prop.json\`); re-mint it from the recipe rather than hand-editing. Target editor: Unreal Engine 5 (5.4+; proven against UE 5.8.0).
#002 Steps marked T are editor actions, one per line, in order. Everything not listed here is done by the importer script — do not set values by hand that the importer already sets.

## ① Open a project

T001 Epic Games Launcher > Unreal Engine > Library > Launch(your installed 5.x) > open your project, or Games > Third Person > Blueprint > Create
T001.01 any 5.4+ editor works; proven against UE 5.8.0; the Third Person template holds the mannequin's IK rig a humanoid figure retargets from

## ② Enable Python

T002 Edit > Plugins > search \`Python Editor Script Plugin\` > Enabled > Restart Now
T002.01 while there, confirm \`Interchange glTF\`(glTF importer) shows Enabled — it is on by default in 5.3+

## ③ Copy the pack in

T003 Finder > copy this whole folder into the project root, beside the \`.uproject\` (for example \`<Project>/Mojulo/sk_test-prop\`) — NOT into \`Content/\`; the importer writes the asset to \`Content/Mojulo/sk_test_prop\` itself

## ④ Run the importer

T004 Window > Output Log > command bar dropdown(currently \`Cmd\`) > \`Python\` > run: \`py Mojulo/sk_test-prop/import_mojulo.py\`
T004.01 Output Log — confirm one line: \`[mojulo] asset sk_test_prop -> /Game/Mojulo/sk_test_prop (preview /Game/Mojulo/sk_test_prop/sk_test_prop_Preview)\`

## ⑤ Look at it — the eyes gate

T005 Content Browser > Content > Mojulo > sk_test_prop > \`sk_test_prop_Preview\` — open
T006 judge with your own eyes:
#003 the asset stands on the floor at its own scale, in its geometry and colours as the mojulo web build shows it (reference look); its materials are mojulo's one vertex-colour material, the light baked into its colours
#004 the figure \`body\` stands skinned (one mesh, its skeleton) and loops its \`idle\` clip
#005 \`Content > Mojulo > sk_test_prop > Retarget\` holds \`IK_Mojulo_body\` (its chains: Spine, LeftArm, LeftLeg, the fingers), and \`RTG_Mojulo_body\` when the project holds the mannequin's rig

Re-export after a change to the recipe and run the importer again: the asset is imported fresh into the same folder, and
a figure's IK Rig and Retargeter are rebuilt in place.
"
`;
